+# ============================================================================
+# The app as a graph. Screens are places a person can be. Edges are how they
+# move and what they do. Control level action nodes are registered at runtime
+# from src/lib/appControls.ts (node id = "do:" + spot id), so every button,
+# tile, row and gesture in the app joins this graph without hand editing.
+#
+# Node kinds (screen meta "kind"):
+#   tab      the five bottom bar tabs
+#   view     a mode inside Checkout (Keypad, All products; Quick Menu is the tab)
+#   page     a pushed route
+#   sheet    a window drawn over the page
+#   overlay  something drawn over everything (sign in, screensaver, practice)
+#   action   a control, a terminal node in a route
+#
+# Edge meta:
+#   say      the words said while pointing at this transition
+#   gesture  tap (default), or a swipe/hold/scroll
+#   spot     the UI spot this transition taps, when it has one
+#   roles    who may take it
+# ============================================================================
+
